<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahmad Khan Muqaddam</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1742">1742</a>–<a href="/years/1806">1806</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahmad Khan Muqaddam was the best-known khan of Maragheh, a small khanate south-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-urmia">Lake Urmia</a> ruled by the Muqaddam family in the 18th century. Like other local khans of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> he kept his own troops, paid tribute to the dominant power of the day and contended with the khans of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/urmia">Urmia</a>, before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajars</a> subdued the region.</p></div>
